   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# SECTION A — BUSINESS CONTEXT AND DATA UNDERSTANDING\n",
    "\n",
    "### A1. Business Context and Problem Definition\n",
    "The City of New York operates the largest municipal government apparatus in the United States, employing over 300,000 public servants across municipal agencies and administering an annual operating budget exceeding **$100 billion**. Personnel remuneration represents the single largest expenditure category in the municipal budget.\n",
    "\n",
    "Within municipal compensation, **overtime expenditure** constitutes a critical fiscal, operational, and managerial challenge:\n",
    "* **Fiscal Volatility & Budgetary Exposure:** Overtime is inherently variable and premium-priced (typically 1.5× base hourly rates). Uncontrolled overtime growth threatens budgetary discipline and diverts capital from essential municipal investments. Across the 12-year period of this dataset (FY2014–FY2025), New York City disbursed **$25.561 billion** in cumulative municipal overtime.\n",
    "* **Operational Scheduling & Workforce Allocation:** Public safety (NYPD, FDNY, Correction) and infrastructure (Sanitation, Transportation, NYCHA) agencies are subject to 24/7/365 minimum-staffing mandates, emergency responses, and statutory service levels. Understanding whether overtime is driven by structural understaffing, seasonal surges, or localized operational bottlenecks is paramount.\n",
    "* **Primary Decision-Makers & Stakeholders:** This analysis is designed for executive decision-makers, specifically:\n",
    "  1. **NYC Office of Management and Budget (OMB):** Evaluating agency budget requests and setting overtime expenditure caps.\n",
    "  2. **NYC Office of the Comptroller:** Auditing public expenditures, assessing fiscal health, and reviewing labor contract compliance.\n",
    "  3. **Agency Commissioners & Chiefs of Department:** Optimizing shift scheduling, fatigue risk management, and staffing deployment.\n",
    "  4. **City Council Committees on Civil Service & Labor:** Evaluating collective bargaining agreements and municipal hiring priorities.\n",
    "* **Decisions Informed by this EDA:**\n",
    "  - Establishing evidence-based agency overtime expenditure thresholds.\n",
    "  - Evaluating the cost-efficiency of permanent headcount expansion versus persistent overtime reliance.\n",
    "  - Designing targeted operational audits for payroll anomalies (such as negative disbursements or zero-hour overtime payments).\n",
    "* **Methodological Boundaries:** This investigation is strictly framed as **descriptive and diagnostic exploratory data analysis (EDA)**. Payroll transaction records document disbursements; they do **not** capture operational shift logs, emergency dispatches, or staffing rosters. Consequently, the dataset alone **cannot establish fraud, employee misconduct, operational inefficiency, or causal mechanisms**. All findings represent observed empirical associations and administrative accounting characteristics.\n"
   ]
  },
