  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "66e41694",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Insight — A2 Dataset Architecture:**\n",
    "1. **Scale and Granularity:** The raw dataset comprises exactly **6,775,830 records across 17 attributes**. Each row represents a specific payroll disbursement record for an individual employee within a municipal agency during a single municipal fiscal year (July 1 through June 30). Because individuals can transfer agencies, change titles, or appear across multiple fiscal years, a row represents a *payroll record* rather than a unique longitudinal individual.\n",
    "2. **Structural Variable Groups:** The 17 columns naturally partition into four functional categories:\n",
    "   - *Temporal & Administrative Identifiers:* `Fiscal Year`, `Payroll Number`, `Agency Name`.\n",
    "   - *Employee & Occupational Classifications:* `Last Name`, `First Name`, `Mid Init`, `Title Description`.\n",
    "   - *Spatial & Organizational Status:* `Work Location Borough`, `Agency Start Date`, `Leave Status as of June 30`.\n",
    "   - *Remuneration & Effort Metrics:* `Base Salary`, `Pay Basis`, `Regular Hours`, `Regular Gross Paid`, `OT Hours`, `Total OT Paid`, `Total Other Pay`.\n",
    "3. **Data Storage & Type Requirements:** Six financial and effort attributes were ingested as text (due to currency formatting and commas) and safely coerced to high-precision 64-bit floating point numbers, while `Fiscal Year` is stored as an integer.\n"
   ]
  },
