  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "134ff4cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Insight — A3 Data Dictionary Governance:**\n",
    "1. **Complete 17-Column Coverage:** Every single column ingested from NYC Open Data is cataloged with its exact technical and business properties. No columns were omitted.\n",
    "2. **Measurement Scale & Incommensurability Warning:** Crucially, `Base Salary` cannot be analyzed as a single unified distribution because its units are dictated by `Pay Basis` (dollars per year vs. dollars per day vs. dollars per hour). Similarly, name masking (`DOE`) prevents individual longitudinal tracking across years, necessitating payroll-record-level and agency-level analytics.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7fab14a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### A4. Primary Analytical Variable: Total Overtime Paid (`Total OT Paid`)\n",
    "**Primary Variable Identification:** `Total OT Paid` is the primary analytical variable for this investigation.\n",
    "* **Variable Definition & Unit:** Continuous numerical monetary variable denominated in nominal United States Dollars ($ USD), representing gross overtime earnings disbursed during the fiscal year.\n",
    "* **Analytical Justification:** Overtime pay represents the primary discretionary, volatile, and premium-priced component of public-sector compensation. In municipal administration, overtime serves as the primary mechanism for meeting mandatory staffing levels and responding to emergencies, but it also represents a potential source of fiscal strain and employee fatigue. Across the twelve fiscal years, the dataset accounts for **$25,560,864,062.73** ($25.561B) in total overtime expenditure.\n",
    "* **Key Properties & Caveats:**\n",
    "  1. *Zero Inflation:* Overtime is highly concentrated; **72.64% of records (4,921,945 records) reflect exactly $0.00 in overtime**, while only **27.30% (1,849,942 records)** reflect positive overtime earnings.\n",
    "  2. *Negative Accounting Adjustments:* Exactly **3,680 records** record negative overtime values (totaling -$1,227,592.31), reflecting administrative clawbacks or retroactive adjustments.\n",
    "  3. *Nominal Valuation:* Payments are recorded in nominal historical dollars and are not adjusted for CPI inflation or contractual cost-of-living increases.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5006e951",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### A5. Supporting Variables, Analytical Expectations, and Excluded Attributes\n",
    "To investigate the drivers, patterns, and organizational context of `Total OT Paid`, six core supporting variables were selected:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Supporting Variable | Variable Type | Analytical Role & Rationale | Initial Analytical Expectation / Hypothesis |\n",
    "| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| **`OT Hours`** | Continuous Numerical | Direct measure of physical overtime effort logged | **Expectation 1:** Strong positive linear correlation ($r > 0.85$) with `Total OT Paid`, with dispersion driven by differing hourly wage rates across titles. |\n",
    "| **`Agency Name`** | Nominal Categorical | Organizational locus of operational deployment | **Expectation 2:** Overtime expenditure is heavily concentrated in frontline emergency services (NYPD, FDNY, Correction, Sanitation) relative to civilian agencies. |\n",
    "| **`Fiscal Year`** | Discrete Temporal | Longitudinal dimension across 12 fiscal periods (FY14–FY25) | **Expectation 3:** Nominal annual overtime expenditure exhibits upward longitudinal growth over the decade, driven by cost-of-living adjustments and operational demands. |\n",
    "| **`Pay Basis`** | Nominal Categorical | Contractual remuneration schedule (Annual, Daily, Hourly) | **Expectation 4:** Uniformed agencies rely predominantly on annual salaried schedules (`Per Annum`), whereas housing/trade agencies rely heavily on daily schedules (`Per Day`). |\n",
    "| **`Work Location Borough`** | Nominal Categorical | Spatial facility deployment across NYC boroughs | **Expectation 5:** Overtime expenditure exhibits localized geographic concentration (e.g. Rikers Island facilities concentrating Correction overtime in Queens). |\n",
    "| **`Regular Gross Paid`** | Continuous Numerical | Baseline compensation earned for standard hours | **Expectation 6:** Overtime acts as a supplementary earnings component for most personnel, but a significant cohort exhibits overtime exceeding 50% of regular base pay. |\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Documented Excluded Columns\n",
    "The following columns are deliberately excluded from downstream predictive or comparative modeling, grounded in data-quality and architectural realities:\n",
    "1. **`Payroll Number`:** Internal administrative agency payroll code; provides redundant organizational information already captured by `Agency Name` and contains 33.87% missing values.\n",
    "2. **`Last Name`, `First Name`, `Mid Init`:** Over 4.38 million records feature redacted/masked names (`DOE`) for public safety and undercover personnel. These fields cannot be used for unique individual tracking and are omitted to maintain privacy compliance.\n",
    "3. **`Agency Start Date`:** Captures appointment date at current agency rather than total civil service seniority or appointment date to current title, limiting its analytical validity for tenure-based wage modeling.\n"
   ]
  },
