    "**Insight — C2 Overtime Hours & Effort Thresholds:**\n",
    "1. **Effort Distribution:** Among the **1,685,052 records with positive hours (24.87%)**, the average physical commitment is **262.79 hours** (median: **200.00 hours**). An annual commitment of 200 overtime hours represents approximately 5 additional weeks of full-time work.\n",
    "2. **Extreme Fatigue Risks:** The top 5% of overtime recipients log over **808.5 hours/year**, and exactly **3,469 records exceed 1,500 overtime hours** (peaking at 3,743 hours). Working 1,500+ overtime hours equates to >30 hours of overtime per week on top of standard work, creating acute physical fatigue risks.\n",
    "3. **Diagnostic Discrepancy:** Exactly **171,966 records exhibit positive overtime payments despite logging 0.0 overtime hours** (totaling $562.77M). These represent lump-sum adjustments, retro payments, or title reclassifications processed under overtime codes, requiring inter-system audit verification.\n"
   ]
