   "source": [
    "**Insight — D2 Categorical Interaction & Structural Labor Divergence:**\n",
    "1. **Statistical Significance:** The Chi-Square Test yields $\\chi^2 = 292,568.61$ ($df = 12, p < 0.001$, Cramer's $V = 0.2625$), overwhelmingly rejecting the null hypothesis of independence between agency and pay basis.\n",
    "2. **Profound Contractual Divergence:** While the uniformed emergency services (Police: 99.54%, Fire: 99.41%, Sanitation: 98.34%, Correction: 97.43%) are virtually 100% structured as annual salaried (`Per Annum`) civil servants, the **NYC Housing Authority (NYCHA)** exhibits a unique labor architecture where **58.48% of personnel are compensated under daily trade schedules (`Per Day`)**.\n",
    "3. **Managerial Implication:** Overtime management policies designed for annual salaried personnel (such as annual FLSA overtime caps) are structurally inapplicable to NYCHA's per diem maintenance workforce.\n"
   ]
