   "source": [
    "**Insight — D3 Institutional Concentration & ANOVA Verification:**\n",
    "1. **Extreme Oligopoly of Overtime:** Municipal overtime is overwhelmingly concentrated in five frontline departments: the Police Department ($9.517B; 37.23%), Fire Department ($4.935B; 19.31%), Department of Correction ($2.795B; 10.93%), Department of Sanitation ($2.060B; 8.06%), and NYCHA ($1.581B; 6.18%). **Together, these top five agencies account for 81.72% ($20.887 billion)** of all citywide overtime outlays.\n",
    "2. **Participation Rate Contrast:** In the top uniformed agencies, overtime participation exceeds **81% to 87%** of personnel, whereas the Department of Education exhibits only **13.63% participation** despite housing 27.4% of citywide headcount.\n",
    "3. **Statistical Significance:** Both One-Way ANOVA ($F = 16,296.16, p < 0.001$) and Kruskal-Wallis ($H = 67,158.41, p < 0.001$) confirm highly significant inter-agency differences.\n"
   ]
