   "source": [
    "**Insight — D4 Longitudinal Overtime Doubling:**\n",
    "1. **Nominal Outlay Doubling (+99.41%):** Annual municipal overtime expenditures virtually doubled from **$1.534 billion in FY2014 to $3.059 billion in FY2024 (+99.41%)**, before recording $2.922 billion in FY2025.\n",
    "2. **Stable Participation vs. Escalating Intensity:** The proportion of records receiving overtime remained remarkably stable across twelve years (fluctuating tightly between **24.0% and 30.4%**). However, the **average disbursement per positive recipient escalated by +79.17%**, rising from **$10,838.35 in FY2014 to $19,418.77 in FY2024**, and reaching a peak of **$20,923.10 in FY2025**. Across all records, average overtime grew from $3,010.86 to $5,434.80 (+80.51%).\n",
    "3. **Managerial Driver:** Long-term overtime expenditure expansion is primarily driven by rising wage rates and increased overtime hours per recipient, rather than expanding the proportion of employees working overtime.\n"
   ]
  },
