   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### D-Final: Ranked Relationship and Driver Summary\n",
    "Based on the bivariate statistical analyses, four core empirical associations govern municipal overtime in New York City:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Rank | Bivariate Relationship | Variable Types | Test Statistic / Evidence | Analytical Finding & Direction | Managerial Implication & Caveat |\n",
    "| :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| **1** | **`Total OT Paid` × `OT Hours`** | Numerical × Numerical | Pearson $r = 0.9133$<br>Spearman $\\rho = 0.9579$ | Exceptionally strong positive physical effort linkage; fan dispersion reflects title hourly base rates ($20.84/hr to $98.35/hr). | Primary physical driver; hours monitoring provides direct expenditure control. Caveat: Non-causal accounting linkage. |\n",
    "| **2** | **`Total OT Paid` × `Agency Name`** | Numerical × Categorical | ANOVA $F = 16,296.16$<br>Kruskal $H = 67,158.41$ | Top 5 agencies account for 81.72% ($20.887B) of all overtime; participation reaches 82–87% in emergency services. | Fiscal oversight must target the top 5 uniformed agencies. Caveat: Driven by 24/7 public safety mandates. |\n",
    "| **3** | **`Total OT Paid` × `Fiscal Year`** | Numerical × Temporal | Outlays: $1.534B $\\rightarrow$ $3.059B<br>Avg: $10,838 $\\rightarrow$ $19,418 | Outlays nominally doubled (+99.41%) driven by +79.17% expansion in payment intensity per recipient. | Expenditure escalation reflects wage and intensity growth. Caveat: Nominal dollars unadjusted for inflation. |\n",
    "| **4** | **`Agency Name` × `Pay Basis`** | Categorical × Categorical | $\\chi^2 = 292,568.61$<br>$df = 12, p < 0.001$ | Uniformed agencies are >97% annual salaried; NYCHA is 58.48% daily per diem trade labor. | Overtime rules must accommodate per diem trade structures. Caveat: Large sample elevates chi-square magnitude. |\n"
   ]
