   "source": [
    "### F3. Top 3–5 Ranked Drivers and Explanatory Factors\n",
    "1. **Institutional Mission & Minimum Staffing Mandates:** The operational requirement to maintain 24/7 staffing in emergency and custodial facilities (NYPD, FDNY, Correction, Sanitation) is the primary organizational determinant of overtime expenditure (accounting for 81.72% of citywide outlays).\n",
    "2. **Physical Labor Hours Commitment:** Physical overtime hours worked represent the primary physical determinant of payment ($r = 0.9133$), with recipient personnel working a median of 200 hours and a severe fatigue cohort logging >1,500 hours.\n",
    "3. **Baseline Wage Rate Multipliers:** Because overtime is compensated at premium rates derived from contractual base pay, higher-paid senior personnel generate disproportionate expenditure per overtime hour ($28.24/hr in <$50k tier vs. $91.60/hr in >$150k tier).\n",
    "4. **Escalating Payment Intensity:** Longitudinal expenditure doubling (+99.41%) was driven primarily by increasing compensation per overtime recipient (+79.17%) rather than workforce expansion.\n"
   ]
