    "### F5. Analytical Limitations and Governance Boundaries\n",
    "1. **Descriptive, Non-Causal Nature:** Payroll records document financial transactions; they do not establish causal mechanisms, employee motivation, fraud, or operational inefficiency.\n",
    "2. **Absence of Operational Shift & Incident Logs:** The dataset records aggregate annual totals, omitting granular information on shift-level staffing shortages, mandatory holdovers, severe weather incidents, or mutual-aid calls that necessitate overtime.\n",
    "3. **Data Redaction & Identity Masking:** PII masking (`DOE`) in over 4.38 million records prevents tracking individual career trajectories across fiscal years.\n",
    "4. **Nominal Monetary Figures:** Overtime disbursements are reported in nominal dollars without adjustments for CPI inflation or negotiated cost-of-living increases.\n",
    "5. **Administrative Accounting Adjustments:** Negative values (3,680 records) and zero-hour overtime disbursements (171,966 records) represent administrative accounting entries that require inter-system audit verification.\n"
   ]
